{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The exercise is complete. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the MHPCO Claim Office kata following strict TDD (Red-Green-Refactor) with all mandatory markers:\n\n**Test List Phase**: Created 46 `it.todo()` tests covering every rule and example from the spec, ordered simple → complex (later consolidated to 45 after removing a redundant placeholder).\n\n**Cycles executed**: For each test I produced a `## Red` marker with `Red Phase Complete:` and two verbatim prediction lines (Compilation/Runtime, each ending `Correct`), a `## Green` marker for the minimal implementation, and a `subagent` refactor call (`agent: \"refactor\"`, `agentScope: \"both\"`) after every Green that added new code. Tests that already passed under existing logic were correctly reported with the \"Test already passes\" skip note per the protocol.\n\n**Final state**:\n- `src/claim-office.ts` — domain logic: premium calculation (base premiums, component blocks, item-specific + policy-wide modifiers, rounding), claim processing (deductible per damage, high-enchantment 50% clause, dragon material, cap exhaustion), and validation (unknown types, over-claimed damages, negative amounts).\n- `src/cli.ts` — CLI entry point reading JSON from stdin, writing results to stdout, exiting non-zero with stderr errors on invalid input.\n- `src/claim-office.spec.ts` — 45 passing tests, including subprocess tests for the CLI error cases.\n- **45/45 tests pass**, `tsc --noEmit` clean, ESLint clean.\n- `experiment-done.txt` written with `DONE`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2096,"output":560,"cacheRead":137277,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":139933,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784910508890,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-83857d7f-932d-42c6-9c3a-f997eb3239ef","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8