ct\n**Runtime Prediction**: premium 88 (3×25 individual) vs 71 (block) Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected.\n\n## Green -- component block pricing: 3 alike components = 60\n\nI need to group components by type and price blocks of 3 at 60. Minimal: separate component pricing. Components are runes (and moonstones later). Let me compute base premium accounting for blocks."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_013EKkeRMxkV3qQVhXntXXw5","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\"]);\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\n// A building block of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike components is offered at a\n// special base premium; leftover components are priced individually.\nconst componentBasePremium = (count: number): number => {\n  const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n  const leftovers = count % BLOCK_SIZE;\n  return blocks * BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM + leftovers * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst baseTotalForItems = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const componentCount = items.filter(isComponent).length;\n  const mainTotal = mainItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemBasePremium(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  return mainTotal + componentBasePremium(componentCount);\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const baseTotal = baseTotalForItems(items);","oldText":"const itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const baseTotal = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemBasePremium(item), 0);"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}}],