ash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | grep -i \"failed\\|passed\\|todo\" | head"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1317,"output":146,"cacheRead":46679,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":48142,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909029496,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e47d0a37-a780-43ac-b890-6e55c8dc1fda","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016XUSrEkhF6N9rJ79AgpKEP","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  8 passed | 38 todo (46)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909033172},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: 8 passing. Refactor."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019hsRmPFwpmuw4QZ73TYXY5","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Changed componentsBasePremium so a block only applies when count is EXACTLY 3 (BLOCK_SIZE); otherwise all components priced individually.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1501,"output":260,"cacheRead":46679,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":48440,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909033175,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-24d7fca4-9436-4d6f-b30d-f37ca03cc02f","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_019hsRmPFwpmuw4QZ73TYXY5","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 8 tests still green.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Naming Evaluation**: All function names (`quotePremium`, `baseTotalForItems`, `itemBasePremium`, `isComponent`, `componentsBasePremium`) already reveal intent clearly. Introduced `sumBasePremiums` — a name that precisely states what it does. No renames of existing functions were needed.\n\n**Refactoring Applied** (Rule 3 — No Duplication, the driving rule):\n1. **Eliminated conceptual duplication**: Removed the `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25` constant, which silently duplicated `BASE_PREMIUMS.rune = 25`. A rune's individual price now has a single source of truth (`BASE_PREMIUMS`). Previously a change to rune pricing would have required updating two places or risked drift.\n2. **Extracted `sumBasePremiums` helper**: Both main-items and (now) individually-priced components sum base premiums via `itemBasePremium`. The shared reduce logic is consolidated into one function, removing the copy-paste summation pattern.\n\nAs a side benefit, `componentsBasePremium` now correctly prices non-block components by their *actual* base premium rather than assuming every component costs 25 — a latent bug that would surface once other component types (e.g. moonstones) are added per the todo tests.\n\n**APP Mass** (affected region): before ≈ **41**, after ≈ **38** (delta −3). The removed constant, removed local `mainTotal` assignment binding, and the removal of the `count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM` multiplication offset the small cost of the new invocation in `sumBasePremiums`. Net mass reduced while clarity and correctness improved.\n\n**Tests**: All 8 passing (38 todo)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Changed componentsBasePremium so a block only applies when count is EXACTLY 3 (BLOCK_SIZE); otherwise all components priced individually.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Changed componentsBasePremium so a block only applies when count is EXACTLY 3 (BLOCK_SIZE); otherwise all components priced individually.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909038750},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01PRixyiDABBAZ2H15YBqKDG","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016RXMFb94NymJA62yEBzjEu","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":222,"output":259,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10185,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909038771,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-932cff3c-51f8-4257-8c7b-4e0749621a13","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01PRixyiDABBAZ2H15YBqKDG","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: unknown[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n};\n\n// Premiums are rounded up in MHPCO's favor. The epsilon absorbs floating-point\n// noise so that mathematically-whole totals are not pushed to the next integer.\nconst roundUpInFavorOfMHPCO = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount - 1e-9);\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_MULTIPLIER = 1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\"]);\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\n// A building block is offered only when there are EXACTLY BLOCK_SIZE alike\n// components; otherwise every component is priced individually.\nconst componentsBasePremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst baseTotalForItems = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const components = items.filter(isComponent);\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const mainTotal = mainItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemBasePremium(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  return mainTotal + componentsBasePremium(components.length);\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const baseTotal = baseTotalForItems(items);\n  // The first-insurance surcharge is a policy-wide modifier applied to the\n  // whole policy's base total, not to individual items.\n  const withFirstInsurance = baseTotal * FIRST_INSURANCE_MULTIPLIER;\n  return roundUpInFavorOfMHPCO(withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909041679},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016RXMFb94NymJA62yEBzjEu","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums / edge cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"single sword -> base 100 G + 5 fee = 105 G (newcomer: +10% first? see integration) - simplest: long-standing established\");\n\n  // --- Item values and base premiums (each main item) ---\n  it(\"sword base premium 100 G (newcomer plain sword: 100 +10% first +5 fee = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"amulet base premium 60 G (newcomer: 60 +10% +5 = 71)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"staff base premium 80 G (newcomer: 80 +10% +5 = 93)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"potion base premium 40 G (newcomer: 40 +10% +5 = 49)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (newcomer: 50 +10% +5 = 60)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies; newcomer: 60 +10% +5 = 71)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - requires exactly 3; newcomer: 100 +10% +5 = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers (item-specific) ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword adds 50% risk surcharge on item base\");\n  it.todo(\"highly enchanted item (enchantment >= 5) adds 30% surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 5 -> both surcharges apply\");\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers (policy-wide) ---\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer (>=2 years) receives 20% loyalty discount\");\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"first insurance carries 10% initial assessment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"15% discount on each contract after the first (follow-up)\");\n  it.todo(\"5 G processing fee added to every premium\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60): base 160, curse adds 50 (50% of sword base) -> 210 before further modifiers/fee\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"intermediate amounts kept as fractions; only final rounded\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3): premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing (3yr) second contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7): premium 160 G\");\n\n  // --- Insurance sum & cap ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"policy sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + 3 runes (block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (block affects premium only)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune (value 250), damage 200 -> payout 100 (no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: special clauses ---\n  it.todo(\"high-enchantment (>=8): dragon sword ench 8 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon material: fully reimbursed\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses, 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 5 damage 800 -> payout 700 (only dragon clause, full then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (only high-ench, 50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of same type ---\n  it.todo(\"two swords, dragon attack damages both (two sword entries) -> each own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damage entries of a type than covered (2 sword damages, 1 sword insured) -> reject, non-zero exit\");\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\"sword (cap 2000), two claims 1500 each -> first payout 1400 remaining 600; second payout 600 remaining 0\");\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit, error on stderr, no results on stdout\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> non-zero exit, error on stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount -200 -> non-zero exit, error on stderr\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909041679},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll run the tests to check if everything is working correctly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01DGj1HMwxLZ6SMYTkjJ2bdt","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":4311,"output":144,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14159,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909041680,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0dcb8936-71d9-4b0