e yet). But to be safe, only count quote steps. Since Step type is only QuoteStep now, all steps are quotes. Let me keep it but note claims will come. For now it works."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AXErod7HsmGLGPK6ifhxHF","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | grep -i \"failed\\|passed\\|todo\" | head"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2187,"output":381,"cacheRead":76502,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":79070,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909542325,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b28660ba-7f68-42c9-9e2d-c7449256f34e","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01AXErod7HsmGLGPK6ifhxHF","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  20 passed | 26 todo (46)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909548755},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: 20 passing. Refactor."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014d4bL78CWHFG4isevbFdXW","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Added 15% follow-up contract discount (any quote after the first in a scenario). Introduced QuoteContext { customer, isFollowUp }; runScenario tracks quoteCount to determine follow-up. Note: claim steps will be added later (Step is currently only QuoteStep); the quoteCount logic currently counts every step.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Do not add claim handling yet (no test drives it).\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1926,"output":333,"cacheRead":77182,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":79441,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909548757,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-06b2929f-2fe9-4d5f-99ab-384f9e2a25ab","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014d4bL78CWHFG4isevbFdXW","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 20 tests still pass.\n\n### Step 5: Refactored Code Mass\n\n```typescript\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step, index) => ({\n    premium: quotePremium(step.items, {\n      customer: scenario.customer,\n      isFollowUp: index > 0,\n    }),\n  }));\n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\nComponent count:\n- Constants: `0` (in `index > 0`) = 1\n- Bindings: results, step, index, scenario, customer, scenario.steps ≈ 6\n- Invocations: `map`, `quotePremium`, `>` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Loops: `map` = 5\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\n**Total Mass ≈ 18**\n\n**Mass Change: ~35 → ~18 (delta ~17)**\n\n### Step 6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** Removed the mutable `quoteCount` binding and its two assignments (`= 0`, `+= 1`), which were speculative machinery for future claim steps not yet driven by any test.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Replaced the side-effecting counter-in-`.map` with `.map`'s `index` parameter. `isFollowUp: index > 0` directly states \"any quote after the first,\" and the map callback becomes a pure expression with no side effects.\n- **APP:** Mass dropped ~35 → ~18, driven almost entirely by eliminating two mutating assignments (mass 6 each).\n\nThe comment was preserved/updated to note the current assumption (every step is a quote), so when claim steps arrive later, the follow-up logic can be revisited deliberately rather than silently.\n\n### Step 7: Report\n\n**Refactoring Complete**\n- **Refactoring**: Replaced mutable `quoteCount` counter with `.map` index; removed side effects and two assignments from `runScenario`.\n- **Mass Change**: ~35 → ~18 (delta ~17)\n- **Tests**: All 20 passing (26 todo untouched)\n- **Claim handling**: Not added — no test drives it, as instructed."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Added 15% follow-up contract discount (any quote after the first in a scenario). Introduced QuoteContext { customer, isFollowUp }; runScenario tracks quoteCount to determine follow-up. Note: claim steps will be added later (Step is currently only QuoteStep); the quoteCount logic currently counts every step.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Do not add claim handling yet (no test drives it).\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 20\nRecent Green phase: Added 15% follow-up contract discount (any quote after the first in a scenario). Introduced QuoteContext { customer, isFollowUp }; runScenario tracks quoteCount to determine follow-up. Note: claim steps will be added later (Step is currently only QuoteStep); the quoteCount logic currently counts every step.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Do not add claim handling yet (no test drives it).\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909553802},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the implementation and test files to understand the current state."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014pw2aMKH3dA5heYu3HRAcs","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Mwncp9zcwa4P59ZArYy7rM","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":295,"output":266,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10265,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909553821,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bfd089a1-5a59-487b-b895-acbcd34b4db7","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014pw2aMKH3dA5heYu3HRAcs","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: unknown[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n// Premiums are rounded up in MHPCO's favor. The epsilon absorbs floating-point\n// noise so that mathematically-whole totals are not pushed to the next integer.\nconst roundUpInFavorOfMHPCO = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount - 1e-9);\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemBasePremium(item), 0);\n\nconst groupByType = (items: Item[]): Item[][] => {\n  const groups = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const group = groups.get(item.type) ?? [];\n    group.push(item);\n    groups.set(item.type, group);\n  }\n  return [...groups.values()];\n};\n\n// A building block is offered only when there are EXACTLY BLOCK_SIZE alike\n// (same-type) components; otherwise items are priced individually at their own\n// base premiums. \"Alike\" means the same component type. Grouping all items by\n// type in a single pass keeps the block rule in one place: a group qualifies\n// for the block price only when it is a component type of exactly BLOCK_SIZE.\nconst qualifiesForBlock = (group: Item[]): boolean =>\n  group.length === BLOCK_SIZE && isComponent(group[0]);\n\nconst groupBasePremium = (group: Item[]): number =>\n  qualifiesForBlock(group) ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM : sumBasePremiums(group);\n\nconst baseTotalForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  groupByType(items).reduce(\n    (total, group) => total + groupBasePremium(group),\n    0,\n  );\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\n// Each risk modifier is a rate applied to the item's base premium, gated by a\n// condition. Modelling them as a list keeps every surcharge rule in one place\n// and makes the total an additive sum of the applicable rates.\nconst isCursed = (item: Item): boolean => item.cursed === true;\nconst isHighlyEnchanted = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst SURCHARGE_RULES: { applies: (item: Item) => boolean; rate: number }[] = [\n  { applies: isCursed, rate: CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE },\n  { applies: isHighlyEnchanted, rate: HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE },\n];\n\nconst itemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = itemBasePremium(item);\n  return SURCHARGE_RULES.filter((rule) => rule.applies(item)).reduce(\n    (surcharge, rule) => surcharge + base * rule.rate,\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\n// Item-level surcharges are risk modifiers charged per item (e.g. the curse\n// surcharge). Summing them here mirrors baseTotalForItems so quotePremium can\n// read as a set of independently-named, additive policy components.\nconst surchargeTotalForItems = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharge(item), 0);\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst isLongStanding = (customer: Customer): boolean =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n\n// Policy-wide modifiers are rates applied to the whole policy's base total,\n// gated by a condition on the customer. A positive rate is a surcharge, a\n// negative rate a discount. Modelling them as a list (mirroring\n// SURCHARGE_RULES) keeps every policy-level rule in one place and makes the\n// total an additive sum of the applicable rates.\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\n// Everything needed to evaluate policy-wide modifiers for one quote: the\n// customer plus whether this is a follow-up (any quote after the customer's\n// first in the scenario).\ninterface QuoteContext {\n  customer: Customer;\n  isFollowUp: boolean;\n}\n\nconst POLICY_MODIFIER_RULES: {\n  applies: (context: QuoteContext) => boolean;\n  rate: number;\n}[] = [\n  { applies: () => true, rate: FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE },\n  { applies: (c) => isLongStanding(c.customer), rate: -LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE },\n  { applies: (c) => c.isFollowUp, rate: -FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE },\n];\n\nconst policyModifierTotal = (baseTotal: number, context: QuoteContext): number =>\n  POLICY_MODIFIER_RULES.filter((rule) => rule.applies(context)).reduce(\n    (total, rule) => total + baseTotal * rule.rate,\n    0,\n  );\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[], context: QuoteContext): number => {\n  const baseTotal = baseTotalForItems(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = surchargeTotalForItems(items);\n  const policyModifiers = policyModifierTotal(baseTotal, context);\n  return roundUpInFavorOfMHPCO(\n    baseTotal + itemSurcharges + policyModifiers + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n    quoteCount += 1;\n    return {\n      premium: quotePremium(step.items, {\n        customer: scenario.customer,\n        isFollowUp,\n      }),\n    };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909557078},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Mwncp9zcwa4P59ZArYy7rM","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums / edge cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"single sword -> base 100 G + 5 fee = 105 G (newcomer: +10% first? see integration) - simplest: long-standing established\");\n\n  // --- Item values and base premiums (each main item) ---\n  it(\"sword base premium 100 G (newcomer plain sword: 100 +10% first +5 fee = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"amulet base premium 60 G (newcomer: 60 +10% +5 = 71)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"staff base premium 80 G (newcomer: 80 +10% +5 = 93)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"potion base premium 40 G (newcomer: 40 +10% +5 = 49)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (newcomer: 50 +10% +5 = 60)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies; newcomer: 60 +10% +5 = 71)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - requires exactly 3; newcomer: 100 +10% +5 = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium (no block; newcomer: 175 +10% +5 = 197.5 -> 198)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })) }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types; newcomer: 75 +10% +5 = 88)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks; newcomer: 120 +10% +5 = 137)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers (item-specific) ---\n  it(\"cursed sword adds 50% risk surcharge on item base (newcomer: 100 +50 curse +10 first +5 = 165)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it(\"highly enchanted item (enchantment >= 5) adds 30% surcharge (newcomer sword ench 5: 100 +30 +10 first +5 = 145)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 145 });\n  });\n  it(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies (newcomer: 145)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 145 });\n  });\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge (newcomer: 100 +10 first +5 = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"cursed sword with enchantment 5 -> both surcharges apply (newcomer: 100 +50 +30 +10 first +5 = 195)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 195 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers (policy-wide) ---\n  it(\"long-standing customer (>=2yr) receives 20% loyalty discount (5yr sword: 100 +10 first -20 loyalty +5 = 95)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies (2yr sword: 95)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"first insurance carries 10% initial assessment surcharge (newcomer sword: 100 +10 +5 = 115)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"15% discount on each contract after the first (0yr, 2nd quote sword: 100 +10 first -15 followup +5 = 100)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 100 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"5 G processing fee added to every premium\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60): base 160, curse adds 50 (50% of sword base) -> 210 before further modifiers/fee\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n  it.todo(\"intermediate amounts kept as fractions; only final rounded\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3): premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing (3yr) second contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7): premium 160 G\");\n\n  // --- Insurance sum & cap ---\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"policy sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + 3 runes (block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (block affects premium only)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus 100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune (value 250), damage 200 -> payout 100 (no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim processing: special clauses ---\n  it.todo(\"high-enchantment (>=8): dragon sword ench 8 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon material: fully reimbursed\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses, 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 5 damage 800 -> payout 700 (only dragon clause, full then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (only high-ench, 50% then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of same type ---\n  it.todo(\"two swords, dragon attack damages both (two sword entries) -> each own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damage entries of a type than covered (2 sword damages, 1 sword insured) -> reject, non-zero exit\");\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\"sword (cap 2000), two claims 1500 each -> first payout 1400 remaining 600; second payout 600 remaining 0\");\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit, error on stderr, no results on stdout\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> non-zero exit, error on stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount -200 -> non-zero exit, error on stderr\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909557078},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me run the tests to confirm they're green before refactoring."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WfhGyPE4Mwcfb16Jgh5ahw","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":7115,"output":154,"cacheRead":9997,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17266,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909557078,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d67d0676-f77c-41fd-abcf-2dcae2871a08","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01WfhGyPE4Mwcfb16Jgh5ahw","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (46 tests | 26 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  20 passed | 26 todo (46)\n   Start at  16:12:41\n   Duration  163ms (transform 36ms, setup 0ms, collect 31ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 46ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909561325},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the tests are passing, so now I'm looking at the code structure to see if there's anything worth refactoring. The quoteCount logic is working as intended since we only have QuoteStep at the moment. Let me start by reviewing the naming conventions and overall structure to make sure everything is clear and consistent.\n\nLooking at the runScenario function, I notice it's using a mutable quoteCount variable that increments with each step, but it's really only checking whether we're past the first step. Since the map function gives us the index parameter, I can simplify this by using index > 0 directly for the isFollowUp flag instead of maintaining a separate counter. This removes the mutation and makes the code more functional.\n\nThere's a consideration though — the notes mention claim steps will be added later, and the current approach with quoteCount is set up to handle that distinction between quote and claim steps. If I switch to using index, it assumes all steps are quotes, which works now but might need reworking when claims arrive. However, since the instruction is to avoid speculative design and keep things simple until there's an actual need, using the index is the cleaner approach for the current state.\n\nThe real issue is the mutation happening inside the map function — that's an anti-pattern. I could preserve the semantic intent of counting quotes while avoiding the side effect, but given that every step is currently a quote anyway, `index > 0` is simpler and clearer. It removes the mutable binding and keeps the code lean. I'll go with that and add a comment explaining the logic.\n\nNow let me calculate the APP mass for this approach. Counting the components more carefully across the entire function body—I need to tally up the constants like the numeric literals, the variable bindings and references throughout, the assignment operations, and the method invocations like map and quotePremium to get a full before picture.\n\nNow looking at the refactored version, I'm replacing the mutable quoteCount pattern with a cleaner functional approach using map to transform each step into a result object containing the premium calculation, which eliminates the assignments and mutation entirely while keeping the same invocation count.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 20 tests pass. Now let me evaluate the implementation for refactoring.\n\n## Refactoring Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\nI reviewed all names: `runScenario`, `quotePremium`, `baseTotalForItems`, `surchargeTotalForItems`, `policyModifierTotal`, `QuoteContext`, `isFollowUp`, etc. These all clearly reveal intent. The one name introduced in the recent Green phase, `quoteCount`, is where I'll focus — not the name itself, but the mutable-counter mechanism behind it.\n\n### Step 2: Current Code Mass (`runScenario`)\n\n```typescript\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n    quoteCount += 1;\n    return { premium: quotePremium(step.items, { customer: scenario.customer, isFollowUp }) };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\nComponent count:\n- Constants: `0` (init), `0` (compare), `1` (`+= 1`) = 3\n- Bindings: quoteCount(decl), results, step, isFollowUp, quoteCount(use), scenario, customer, isFollowUp(use), scenario.steps ≈ 9\n- Invocations: `map`, `quotePremium`, `>` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Loops: `map` = 5\n- Assignments: `quoteCount = 0` (init), `quoteCount += 1` = 2 × 6 = 12\n\n**Total Mass ≈ 35**\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** ✅ All 20 green.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** The `let quoteCount` + `quoteCount += 1` mutation inside `.map` is a side-effect within a supposedly-pure mapping — a well-known smell. Since `quoteCount` is only ever read as `> 0`, and every step is currently a quote, \"any quote after the first\" is exactly the array position. `index > 0` states that intent directly.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** None found.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** The mutable counter is speculative machinery (anticipating future claim steps that no test drives yet). It adds a binding, two assignments, and a side-effecting map. Removing it in favor of `.map`'s `index` parameter is simpler and drives out complexity that no current test requires.\n\n### Step 4: Implement Refactoring"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01V3YvoqPjc3fnAJgtjSxBDP","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-55-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n    quoteCount += 1;\n    return {\n      premium: quotePremium(step.items, {\n        customer: scenario.customer,\n        isFollowUp,\n      }),\n    };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};","newText":"export const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  // A follow-up is any quote after the customer's first in the scenario. Every\n  // st