ementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 39\nRecent Green phase: Capped payout at policy's remaining cap via Math.min(desiredPayout, policy.remainingCap) in processClaim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Do not add error handling yet (no tests drive it). The remaining todo tests are all error cases (unknown item type, item not in policy, negative amount, too many damage entries) which will be handled in the CLI layer.\n\nRefactor while keeping tests green. Run autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":737,"output":330,"cacheRead":115937,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":117004,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784910078759,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5aafd269-aef6-4421-9442-4c18d162d8cb","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01SiEaDjQ8rMELX4z8Dtw6L7","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 39 tests still green.\n\n### Step 5: Refactored Code Mass (`damagePayout` + new predicate)\n\n```ts\nconst qualifiesForHalfPayout = (item) =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_PAYOUT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst damagePayout = (damage, insuredItem) => {\n  const reimbursed = qualifiesForHalfPayout(insuredItem)\n    ? damage.amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_PAYOUT_RATE\n    : damage.amount;\n  return reimbursed - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n```\n- `qualifiesForHalfPayout`: binding `item` + refs (2) + const `0` (1) + invocation `??`/`>=` (~2) ≈ 6\n- `damagePayout`: bindings/refs (damage, insuredItem, reimbursed, damage.amount x2, RATE, DEDUCTIBLE) ≈ 9; invocations (`qualifiesForHalfPayout()`=2, `*`, `-`) ≈ 4; conditional `?:` = 4 → ≈ 17\n\n**Combined Total Mass ≈ 23**\n\n**Mass Change**: 23 → 23 (delta 0). The dropped `enchantment` local (mass ~3) is offset by the named-predicate invocation (mass